# arch-replay-stop.expect — the required logical behaviour per case, read by neither half.
#
# EXPECT|<case-id>|<admitted>|<classification>|<quarantine>|<targets>|<cursor>|<owed>
#
# The requirement is ARCH-CLOSE-11 with M-5, M-14 and M-17: startup, doctor and recovery validate
# against one recorded policy basis and classify the cause of a refusal before offering repair. A
# recorded row that a missing basis cannot validate leaves the projection it was admitted against
# intact, keeps its continuation owner and its owed delivery, and enters no quarantine, because
# nothing establishes that the row's bytes are corrupt. A row whose own binding no longer recomputes
# is a different cause with a different disposition: the refused bytes are preserved and the row does
# not fold. `targets` is the number of target tasks the projection binds after the case; `cursor` is
# the last sequence the projection covers; `owed` is the rows past the reader cursor.
EXPECT|stop-policy-bearing|true|none|false|2|3|2
EXPECT|stop-missing-policy|false|missing_policy_basis|false|0|2|1
EXPECT|stop-corrupt-row|false|corrupt_source_bytes|true|0|2|1
